# Audit report -- Phase 281: a hash label written in prose is not a field

**Verdict**: PASS
**Target**: docs/plan-qor-phase281-dialect-prose-over-read.md (iteration 9)
**Session**: 2026-09-08T2348-16c62e
**Issues**: GH #428
**Mode**: adversarial; nine review rounds, independent reviewer, every load-bearing claim re-measured from source
**Iterations**: 9 (eight prior VETOs)
**Risk Grade**: L1 -- two regex constants and one `re.compile`; no function grows, no signature changes, no security path

## Scope

`ledger_dialect` admitted arbitrary text between a hash label and its value, so a
label quoted inside a sentence was read as a field and narrative text could
displace an entry's real digest. The fix adds a line anchor and a restricted
connective to `_field_re` only. `_HASH_VALUE`, `_label_re` and `SESSION_SEAL_RE`
are untouched.

